  <BetterInspectPane.PawnShowSkills>Show Pawn skills (skill level bars below the regular bar area)</BetterInspectPane.PawnShowSkills>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTooltip>Skill bar tooltips</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTooltip>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTooltipTip>When enabled, hovering a skill bar shows the vanilla character tab skill tooltip (skill description, current level, xp progress, learning speed, etc., identical to the vanilla tooltip).</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTooltipTip>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillPlainText>Plain text skill style</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillPlainText>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillPlainTextTip>When enabled, skill entries draw only the skill name and level text, without the bar background and progress fill (passion display and tooltips are unaffected; the white font toggle has no effect in this style).</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillPlainTextTip>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillShowProgressText>Show xp progress in skill level</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillShowProgressText>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillShowProgressTextTip>When enabled, the skill level is shown in fixed two-decimal format with the xp progress within the current level: e.g. level 5 + 55% progress = 5.55, level 5 + 5% = 5.05, whole / max levels also carry decimals = 5.00 / 20.00. When disabled, the integer level is shown.</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillShowProgressTextTip>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillWhiteFont>Skill bar text in white</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillWhiteFont>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillWhiteFontTip>When enabled, the skill name and level on skill bars always render in white, ignoring the fill ratio (embedded text no longer turns black over the filled area); when disabled, the fill-contrast mask is used (white on the unfilled part, black over the filled part).</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillWhiteFontTip>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTotalProgress>Fill skill bars by total progres</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTotalProgress>

  <BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTotalProgressTip>When enabled, the skill bar fill ratio = (current level + current xp progress) / skill level cap 20, e.g. level 10.5 shows as 52.5%; when disabled, only the xp progress within the current level is shown (bar is empty right after leveling up from 0).</BetterInspectPane.PawnSkillTotalProgressTip>

