  <BetterInspectPane.EnableSelectionLimitModify_Tip>When enabled, a slider appears to set the maximum number of objects you can select at once. The vanilla game hard-codes this to 200; the change applies to both clicking and drag-box selection.</BetterInspectPane.EnableSelectionLimitModify_Tip>
  <BetterInspectPane.SelectionLimit>Selection count limit: {0}</BetterInspectPane.SelectionLimit>

  <BetterInspectPane.EnableImprovedShiftSelection>Improved vanilla Shift selection</BetterInspectPane.EnableImprovedShiftSelection>
  <BetterInspectPane.EnableImprovedShiftSelection_Tip>Changes how holding Shift changes the selection.
•  Drag-box: when the current priority (colonists → humanlikes → resources → pawns → selectable) only matches objects that are already selected, it falls through to the next priority instead of stopping, so new objects of a lower priority can still be added.
•  Clicking: if the clicked object is of a different type than your current selection (e.g. you have pawns selected and Shift-click a zone, which in vanilla would clear the pawns), that selection is ignored and your current selection is kept.</BetterInspectPane.EnableImprovedShiftSelection_Tip>

  <BetterInspectPane.EnableCtrlSelection>Ctrl selection (Ctrl + drag)</BetterInspectPane.EnableCtrlSelection>
  <BetterInspectPane.EnableCtrlSelection_Tip>When holding Ctrl and drag-boxing, selection depends on your current selection:
• Nothing selected: select all of the player's pawns in the box; if none, all of the player's turret buildings; if none, all buildings; if none, vanilla behavior.
• One or more selected (based on the first one): incrementally add all similar objects in the box (vanilla similarity: same def and faction, or equivalent pawns); if nothing new was added, select by the base object's type — zone → all zones, pawn → all pawns of the same faction, building → all buildings of the same faction, resource → all resources, otherwise → all non-pawn non-resource non-building selectables; if still nothing, vanilla behavior.
Holding Ctrl never clears the current selection.</BetterInspectPane.EnableCtrlSelection_Tip>

  <BetterInspectPane.EnableRememberOpenTab>Remember the open inspect tab</BetterInspectPane.EnableRememberOpenTab>
  <BetterInspectPane.EnableRememberOpenTab_Tip>When enabled, after switching target types closes the inspect tab, re-selecting the same type of target will auto-open the previously opened tab if it can still be opened.
• Remembers the last N target types (a type is determined by the tabs it can open), where N is the capacity set by the slider below (2-10, default 2); e.g. with capacity 2, after A→B→C→A the memory of A is lost.
• Manually closing a tab won't re-open it immediately; it only auto-opens when you switch to another type and then back.</BetterInspectPane.EnableRememberOpenTab_Tip>
